A||N||3||Wudman||Paid your gas bill lately? Are you mad yet?||||1||
Z||000000||Wudman||01-30-2001||03:09 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.thisisfun.com/fighthighgas/fhgp1.jpg">  <BR> <BR><B>What is it going to take make you really angry?</B> Is it the last time you<BR>gassed your car or paid gas bill? If not, it is time for you, my fellow<BR>citizens to show up! Energy costs are moving back into the area of very<BR>abusive. Natural gas is already there and in St.. Louis it went up an addtional 29% this month! Gasoline is inching up, but I suspect we will really get hammered this spring! Here we are, deep in winter, gas is .50 more than a year ago this time and the<BR>forecast is for higher prices! I don't even want to see what happens this summer! If we see a spike like last year, $3.00 a gallon is guaranteed in many areas of the US!<P><B>By the way, there is more gasoline in inventory now than a year ago, yet the price is 30% higher! Maybe that has something to do with the 80% higher profits shown by producers in 2000?</B> <BR>Listen folks, it is easier to stop a car rolling down the hill before it<BR>gets any momentum! If we are to have any chance at influencing prices,<BR>policy and our economies, we have to try now.<BR>It is time to re-live and re-learn the lessons that OPEC taught us once<BR>already in the 70's.<BR>Conserve, consolidate your driving, spend gas like it was gold and pass the<BR>word up the chain of representation.<P>As a fellow citizen and Fiero owner, I ask you to use your e-mail, websites and<BR>phone, to get the word out! SPAM your mayor, Congressman, and of course our oil company loving President. I have posted on my website, links that will get you the e-mail of just about any government official. Spam your friends and implore them to do the same. It has to start somewhere, and now is getting late. We have few choices, but to wait around and see how big a hosing we are going to have to accommodate is a stupid,<BR>lazy one. At least if they screw us this summer as they are this winter and last summer, we can say we tried. More importantly we can show that we are not some lambs that are going to just softly bleat as they shove us in the grinder a little further.<P>I hope that we can awaken as a group now! The whimper we let out last summer<BR>was not enough.<P>Bottom line, big oil, OPEC, our waste and bad habits are crafting an environment that is busting us! Enough said today. Spread the Rant!<P>Wudman<BR>S. IL<BR><A HREF="http://www.thisisfun.com/fighthighgas/fhg.htm" TARGET=_blank>Fight High Gas Prices!</A><BR>"Call to Action" direct link w/ links to spread your concern!.<BR>P.S. don't be fooled by gas prices that seem to be hovering right now, demand for gas is historically low this time of year. Once it warms up, we are going to get hosed like never before! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.thisisfun.com/banners/sprdthewrd.gif">   <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Wudman (edited 01-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||02-01-2001||11:17 AM||||If every car in America had properly inflated tires, properly tuned engines, and drivers who drove the speed limit and eliminated unnecessary trips, there would be no gas crisis.<P>I myself do all of the above things except the unnecessary trip thing.<P>As to natural gas, I just knew if I kept that "Eat Beans, America needs the Gas" T-shirt long enough, it'd be in style again.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||02-01-2001||03:06 PM||||i just paid a $154 gas bill for my house!  in three years of ownership, the most i had ever paid was $75!<P>whats worse yet, is that not once, in the whole month was my house actually warm!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wudman||02-01-2001||05:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B>i just paid a $154 gas bill for my house!  in three years of ownership, the most i had ever paid was $75!<P>whats worse yet, is that not once, in the whole month was my house actually warm!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Just imagine, the reaming going on in regards to the natural gas prices is just the beginning. Because of the crap going down west, that joke called deregulation and greed, our electricity rates will be going sky high. (If not directly in relation to the shortage, chalk it up to the pending "public" utiolity bail out or the fact that lots of electrcity is generated  natural gas!)<BR>In regards to home heating, my dear old retired Grandfather's bill doubled to $500 in December, not LaClede gas just raised prices an additional 29%. Hmmm, $500+29%=$645 to heat his house. (yeah, his boiler is ancient)<BR>God bless dead trees and wood stoves!<P>||||reg||1
